{%- comment -%}
  Registry accessor (spec §17.2) — the single indirection every caller uses, so
  caching lives in ONE place. The manifests are CODE (deploy-invariant), and
  platformOS's {% cache %} auto-invalidates on any view/translation change (= on
  deploy), so the built registry is cached across requests and rebuilt only when a
  manifest/registry view actually changes. This removes the per-request manifest
  meta-validation + description-lint from the hot path (registry/load runs on every
  tools/list AND every tools/call via resolve_tool).

  CACHE KEY correctness: the app registry partial conditionally registers the gated
  test/vuln fixtures based on the MCP_ENABLE_TEST_TOOLS / MCP_ENABLE_VULN_TOOLS
  CONSTANTS. A constant change is NOT a view change, so {% cache %} would not
  auto-invalidate on a runtime toggle — therefore the two gate values are folded
  into the key. In production both are unset → one stable key → fully cached; when a
  gate is toggled (CI/eval) the key changes and the correct variant is (re)built.
  `expire` is a defensive TTL only (deploy + gate-key are the real invalidators).

  Cached as a JSON string (the {% cache %} block stores rendered text) and parsed
  back — a byte round-trip of the built hash. No caller changes.

  @return {object} { tools, excluded, count } — see registry/build
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign test_gate = context.constants.MCP_ENABLE_TEST_TOOLS | default: ''
  assign vuln_gate = context.constants.MCP_ENABLE_VULN_TOOLS | default: ''
  assign ckey = 'mcp_registry_v1|' | append: test_gate | append: '|' | append: vuln_gate
-%}
{%- capture reg_json -%}
  {%- cache ckey, expire: 300 -%}
    {%- liquid
      function built = 'modules/mcp/commands/registry/build'
      echo built | json
    -%}
  {%- endcache -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign reg = reg_json | parse_json
  return reg
-%}
